Done. Both changes are implemented, build cleanly, and verified end-to-end.

**What changed:**

1. `rust/src/lib.rs` — Added the public function:
   ```rust
   pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
       notes.iter().filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)).collect()
   }
   ```
   Exact match (`==`), preserves relative order, returns `Vec<&'a Note>`.

2. `rust/src/main.rs` — Wired `--tag <TAG>` into the `list` command. It scans remaining args for `--tag` and takes the next value; when present, output is filtered through `filter_by_tag`, otherwise all notes print.

